{"id":"2dd1386ba4ddb99c","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-df-adjunction.md","title":"Adjunction Formula","display":"df-adjunction — Adjunction Formula","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-adjunction","aliases":["58-df-adjunction"],"display":"df-adjunction — Adjunction Formula","depends_on":["[[../batch03/58-df-canonical-divisor.md]]","[[../batch01/58-df-hypersurface.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-adjunction"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-adjunction</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-adjunction — Adjunction Formula"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3042e345de149e5\" href=\"?note=a3042e345de149e5\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-canonical-divisor.md\">../batch03/58-df-canonical-divisor.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"99574bf9a84bc839\" href=\"?note=99574bf9a84bc839\" title=\"../batch01/58-df-hypersurface.md\">../batch01/58-df-hypersurface.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,Y,n,K_X,K_Y\\in V\">\\(X,Y,n,K_X,K_Y\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S\\)</span> (canonical-divisor predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"a3042e345de149e5\" href=\"?note=a3042e345de149e5\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-canonical-divisor.md\">../batch03/58-df-canonical-divisor.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Hypersurf}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Hypersurf}_S\\)</span> (hypersurface predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"99574bf9a84bc839\" href=\"?note=99574bf9a84bc839\" title=\"../batch01/58-df-hypersurface.md\">../batch01/58-df-hypersurface.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sim\">\\(\\sim\\)</span> (linear equivalence of divisors)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AdjunctionFormula}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{AdjunctionFormula}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}adjunction} \\vdash \\mathrm{AdjunctionFormula}_S(X,Y)\\leftrightarrow \\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\exists K_X,K_Y\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Hypersurf}_S(Y,X,n)\\land\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S(K_X,X)\\land\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S(K_Y,Y)\\land K_Y\\sim(K_X+Y)\\upharpoonright Y\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}adjunction} \\vdash \\mathrm{AdjunctionFormula}_S(X,Y)\\leftrightarrow \\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\exists K_X,K_Y\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Hypersurf}_S(Y,X,n)\\land\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S(K_X,X)\\land\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S(K_Y,Y)\\land K_Y\\sim(K_X+Y)\\upharpoonright Y\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Adjunction computes the canonical divisor of a hypersurface.</li>\n<li>For curves on surfaces: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g(C) = \\frac{1}{2}(C \\cdot C + C \\cdot K) + 1\">\\(g(C) = \\frac{1}{2}(C \\cdot C + C \\cdot K) + 1\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>For plane curves of degree <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d\">\\(d\\)</span>: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g = \\frac{(d-1)(d-2)}{2}\">\\(g = \\frac{(d-1)(d-2)}{2}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Generalizes to complete intersections via excess intersection formula.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch03/58-df-canonical-divisor.md","status":"resolved","id":"a3042e345de149e5","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-df-canonical-divisor.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch01/58-df-hypersurface.md","status":"resolved","id":"99574bf9a84bc839","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch01/58-df-hypersurface.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch03/58-df-canonical-divisor.md","status":"resolved","id":"a3042e345de149e5","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S$ (canonical-divisor predicate, see [[../batch03/58-df-canonical-divisor.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch01/58-df-hypersurface.md","status":"resolved","id":"99574bf9a84bc839","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Hypersurf}_S$ (hypersurface predicate, see [[../batch01/58-df-hypersurface.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X,Y,n,K_X,K_Y\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Hypersurf}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\sim","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{AdjunctionFormula}_S\\subseteq V^2","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}adjunction} \\vdash \\mathrm{AdjunctionFormula}_S(X,Y)\\leftrightarrow \\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\exists K_X,K_Y\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Hypersurf}_S(Y,X,n)\\land\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S(K_X,X)\\land\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S(K_Y,Y)\\land K_Y\\sim(K_X+Y)\\upharpoonright Y\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"g(C) = \\frac{1}{2}(C \\cdot C + C \\cdot K) + 1","display":false},{"tex":"d","display":false},{"tex":"g = \\frac{(d-1)(d-2)}{2}","display":false}],"bytes":1271,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-116","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-adjunction.md|58-df-adjunction]]（batch13）"}],"outgoing":["a3042e345de149e5","99574bf9a84bc839"]}